WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.656
Good morning, it's Friday, November 6.

00:00:02.726 --> 00:00:10.065
This is Signal in the AI Fog, your daily briefing on enterprise AI in production, written and read by AI.

00:00:10.135 --> 00:00:18.802
Today: Model shelf lives keep shrinking, LLMjacking targets enterprise AI keys, and What self-hosting Mistral Large 4 takes.

00:00:18.872 --> 00:00:20.829
First, the story of the day.

00:00:20.899 --> 00:00:25.582
Start with Google's own lifecycle documentation for the Flash line.

00:00:25.652 --> 00:00:33.900
Gemini 3.6 Flash was released July twenty-first and retires November nineteenth on Google's enterprise agent platform.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:40.330
Gemini 3.7 Flash, released August thirteenth, retires there on January twenty-eighth, 2027.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:47.180
Gemini 3.8 Flash, released September second, lists retirement on September second, 2027 or later.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.605
That is three Flash versions in about six weeks.

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:51.933
Pricing moves too.

00:00:52.003 --> 00:01:02.907
Google announced Gemini 4 Carbon on October twenty-eighth at an introductory two dollars per million input tokens and ten dollars per million output tokens.

00:01:02.977 --> 00:01:11.364
Press coverage says a footnote raises these to four dollars and twenty dollars afterwards, and Google has not said when.

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:13.671
Carbon is not on the public API.

00:01:13.741 --> 00:01:21.080
And on a new version of the Artificial Analysis index, ActuIA reports Mistral Large 4 fell from 38 to 25.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:27.199
The bigger picture: three things teams treat as stable all moved this week.

00:01:27.273 --> 00:01:31.468
The model identifier, the price, and the benchmark scale.

00:01:31.541 --> 00:01:36.545
Each is documented, each has a date, and none is under your control.

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:40.078
Treat a model route as a lease, not a purchase.

00:01:40.151 --> 00:01:46.922
Record the release date, retirement date, price basis and index version next to every route.

00:01:46.995 --> 00:01:53.103
Re-run your evaluation set when a replacement appears, not when the notice arrives.

00:01:53.177 --> 00:01:55.311
And negotiate notice periods.

00:01:55.385 --> 00:01:59.800
If the Flash cadence is a guide, this pace likely continues.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.431
Next, Sovereignty and Europe.

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:13.075
According to the blog SmartScope, Mistral Large 4's official weights total about 1060 gigabytes, or about 610 gigabytes in the NVFP4 quantized version.

00:02:13.145 --> 00:02:21.688
It is a mixture of experts with roughly one trillion parameters, about 52 billion active, and a one million token context.

00:02:21.758 --> 00:02:25.890
DataNorth's headline says it needs at least four B200 GPUs.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:31.160
What this really signals: open weights are not the same as operable.

00:02:31.229 --> 00:02:35.419
Even quantized, hundreds of gigabytes means a multi-GPU node.

00:02:35.487 --> 00:02:41.600
For a platform team, sovereign self-hosting is first a capacity and utilization question.

00:02:41.669 --> 00:02:46.820
Compare its all-in cost with a European managed endpoint before committing.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.366
Next, Platform.

00:02:48.429 --> 00:02:53.913
TechRadar reports on findings from Google's Threat Intelligence Group about LLMjacking.

00:02:53.976 --> 00:03:00.721
Attackers steal AI API keys and cloud credentials, then run expensive model workloads on the victim's bill.

00:03:00.784 --> 00:03:11.060
Google saw two clusters coordinating to compromise and monetize enterprise LLM infrastructure, plus so-called LLM Mixers that proxy and resell unauthorized access.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:16.332
Why it matters: a gateway is a spend control, and also a target.

00:03:16.405 --> 00:03:23.706
Per-key budgets, short-lived credentials and alerts on token volume per team are the cheap defenses.

00:03:23.779 --> 00:03:29.400
Test that an alert fires on an overnight spike, not just that a quota exists.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:30.991
Next, Quality.

00:03:31.062 --> 00:03:40.195
In its post accompanying the open weights, Mistral says reinforcement learning lifted Large 4 on the B3 Agent Security Benchmark.

00:03:40.265 --> 00:03:46.000
It resisted 97.1 percent of attacks, against 93.3 percent in the preview version.

00:03:46.071 --> 00:03:51.593
Mistral also says Large 4 now outperforms GLM-5.3 and DeepSeek Flash 4.1 1017.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:54.000
Both are the vendor's own claims.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:04:00.552
Reading between the lines: the same model name scored differently between preview and final.

00:04:00.617 --> 00:04:09.595
Pin the exact version in your evaluation records, and re-run security tests, including your own prompt injection cases, at each checkpoint.

00:04:09.659 --> 00:04:11.920
A vendor benchmark is a hypothesis.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:13.295
A follow-up.

00:04:13.359 --> 00:04:16.674
Expected: Mistral Large 4 live in Microsoft Foundry.

00:04:16.738 --> 00:04:24.579
Mistral's own open-weights post now lists Foundry as a managed route, with private deployment options for Azure developers.

00:04:24.643 --> 00:04:28.723
I still found no Microsoft catalogue page confirming it is live.

00:04:28.787 --> 00:04:30.190
The number of the day.

00:04:30.254 --> 00:04:38.159
Gemini 3.6 Flash was released on July twenty-first and retires on November nineteenth, according to Google's lifecycle page.

00:04:38.223 --> 00:04:41.793
A model's production life can be set by a single notice.

00:04:41.857 --> 00:04:45.491
Budget migration work as a recurring cost, not a one-off.

00:04:45.555 --> 00:04:46.447
What to watch.

00:04:46.511 --> 00:04:51.866
Anthropic's IPO marketing, which reports say could start the week of November ninth.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:54.926
EuroHPC gigafactory bids, due November twelfth.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:05:01.748
Microsoft Ignite from November seventeenth, the same day several Gemini text-to-speech previews shut down.

00:05:01.812 --> 00:05:04.936
Gemini 3.6 Flash retiring on November nineteenth.

00:05:04.999 --> 00:05:08.888
Walmart's Agent Profiles, due by about November twenty-first.

00:05:08.952 --> 00:05:11.120
AI Act marking on December second.

00:05:11.184 --> 00:05:14.116
And any date for wider Gemini 4 Carbon access.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.029
And a question for your team.

00:05:16.093 --> 00:05:27.313
For each model route in production, do you record its retirement date, its price basis and the evaluation version that approved it, and who is alerted when any of them changes?

00:05:27.377 --> 00:05:28.652
That's it for today.

00:05:28.716 --> 00:05:31.202
Sources are in the episode description.

00:05:31.266 --> 00:05:33.179
This was Signal in the AI Fog.

00:05:33.242 --> 00:05:34.390
See you on Monday.
